/-!
# Linear Noether normalization in prescribed generators

Mathlib's Noether normalization theorem (`exists_finite_inj_algHom_of_fg`) works over an arbitrary
field by applying Nagata's nonlinear variable substitutions `X_j ↦ X_j + X_0^{r_j}`. Over an
infinite field `k`, one can instead normalize a nontrivial `k`-algebra `A` generated by a prescribed
tuple `x : Fin n → A` using *linear* combinations `y i = ∑ j, C i j • x j`: there exist `d ≤ n` and
a matrix `C : Matrix (Fin d) (Fin n) k` such that `y` is algebraically independent over `k`,
`MvPolynomial.aeval y : k[X_0, …, X_{d-1}] →ₐ[k] A` is module-finite, and `ringKrullDim A = d`
(`TauCeti.exists_linear_normalization`). By
`AlgebraicIndependent.linearIndependent_of_sum_smul`, the rows of any such matrix `C` are
`k`-linearly independent.

The elimination step holds over an arbitrary commutative ring `R`: if a polynomial `f` vanishes at
`x : Fin (n + 1) → A` and its top homogeneous component takes an invertible value at the direction
`i.insertNth 1 a`, rescaling `MvPolynomial.shearToPolynomial i a f` gives a monic polynomial over
the subalgebra generated by the sheared coordinates `x (i.succAbove j) - a j • x i` with root `x i`
(`TauCeti.isIntegral_adjoin_sub_smul`), making `A` module-finite over that subalgebra when `x`
generates `A` (`TauCeti.finite_adjoin_sub_smul_of_adjoin_eq_top`). Over an infinite field, a good
shear direction always exists (`TauCeti.exists_eval_insertNth_homogeneousComponent_ne_zero`), and
induction on `n` composes the resulting shear matrices.

Because the normalizing generators are linear combinations with coefficients in `k`, the *same*
matrix `C.map (algebraMap k K)` normalizes `K ⊗[k] A` with respect to `(1 : K) ⊗ₜ[k] x j` for every
field extension `K / k` (`TauCeti.linear_normalization_tensorProduct`), without requiring `k` to be
infinite once `C` is given.

The infinite-field hypothesis in `TauCeti.exists_linear_normalization` cannot be omitted: over
`𝔽₂`, the nontrivial algebra `𝔽₂[X_0, X_1] ⧸ (X_0 X_1 (X_0 + X_1))` generated by the residue
classes of `X_0` and `X_1` admits no `d` and no `𝔽₂`-linear combinations `y : Fin d → A` that are
algebraically independent over `𝔽₂` with `A` integral over `𝔽₂[y]`
(`TauCeti.not_exists_linear_normalization_zmod_two`), since the union of all three lines through the
origin in `𝔸²(𝔽₂)` collapses one of those lines onto the origin under every linear projection to
`𝔸¹(𝔽₂)`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.isIntegral_adjoin_sub_smul`: deterministic shear elimination of one generator over an
  arbitrary commutative ring.
* `TauCeti.finite_adjoin_sub_smul_of_adjoin_eq_top`: module-finiteness of `A` over the subalgebra
  generated by the `n` sheared coordinates.
* `TauCeti.exists_linear_normalization`: linear Noether normalization in prescribed generators over
  an infinite field, including `ringKrullDim A = d`.
* `TauCeti.exists_linear_normalization_quotient`: specialization to `MvPolynomial (Fin n) k ⧸ I`
  with its standard coordinate classes.
* `TauCeti.linear_normalization_tensorProduct`: persistence of a linear normalization under an
  arbitrary field extension `K / k`.
* `TauCeti.not_exists_linear_normalization_zmod_two`: counterexample over `𝔽₂` showing sharpness of
  `[Infinite k]`.

## References

* J. S. Milne, *Algebraic Geometry* (v6.10, 2024), Theorem 2.44 and Remark 2.47.
* J. S. Milne, *A Primer of Commutative Algebra*, Theorem 8.3 and Remark 8.4.
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00OW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00OW) and
  [Tag 00GQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00GQ).
-/

